# Nurture email (Brunson plain-letter)

Applies to list and nurture sends. Helpers live in `src/lib/mindy-reignite-emails.mjs` (`B`, `U`, `BU`, `LIST`, `LINK`, `PS`, `shell`). Reuse them. Do not rebuild a template.

This rule does not apply to `src/lib/email.ts` (event and transactional HTML).

Approved 2026-07-01.

- White background, black text (#222), system sans-serif. No gradient header, logo banner, colored pill buttons, or graphics.
- Signed personally: `— Eric`. A letter from a person, not a broadcast.
- Heavy inline emphasis. `<strong>` for key phrases, underline for single words, bold+underline for the gut-punch lines.
- Index lists with `→` arrows (or `*`), 2–3 short items, each with a bolded keyword. Not graphics or bullets.
- P.S. line after the signature (often most-read). Make it a loss-reframe stinger.
- CTA is an underlined text link (`→ Finish my profile`), not a button, plus tiny gray "(takes about two minutes)" under it.
- Voice: fear-of-loss / curiosity, short paragraphs, one idea per line.
- Why: reads personal, higher engagement, better inbox placement. Designed HTML trips Promotions/spam. Plain letters land in Primary.
